-- Import of the LOAN MONITORING 2026 workbook (Paulo, 2026-11-15). Needs
-- 20261121010000_loan_schedule.sql first. Run with Paulo's claims so the audit
-- log names him.
--
-- What is imported:
--   • 5 loans from Stella Garcia (STELL G. LOAN sheet; block Y–AE is a copy of
--     Q–W and is not imported) + Stella's L300 (deposit to Rafael). Paulo: the
--     money was received long ago; no back-tracking on the cash sheet.
--   • Security Bank ₱5M (debited from the Security Bank account), First Circle
--     (paid from Metrobank), L300 Siobal–Garcia (₱21,414 every 5th).
--   • BPI credit line: the two "PROCEED FROM LOAN BPI" cash rows of 2026-09-08
--     (₱1M BDO + ₱2M BPI) are draws; the ₱1M repayment from the Eyesports Nuvali
--     collection (per the sheet; not on the cash sheet, date to confirm); the
--     2026-09-05 "INTEREST BPI CREDIT LINE" row.
-- Installments due on or before 2026-11-15 are recorded as paid "per the loan
-- sheet" (not on the cash sheet): one entry for everything before 2026-08-11
-- (before the cash sheet), one entry per installment after. The Oct and Nov
-- L300 Siobal payments are linked to their cash-sheet rows.
-- The sheet's errors are corrected here: Stella's due dates typed as 2026-01..
-- after 2026-12 are 2027; Security Bank's ₱1-a-month drift; Security Bank's
-- missing 24th payment. Idempotent (on conflict do nothing).
-- ROLLBACK: remove the rows whose id starts with 'loan-' / 'lsch-' / 'lpay-imp-'
--   (Manager), schedule first, then payments, then loans; audit_log keeps them.

select set_config('request.jwt.claims', '{"username":"paulo","user_role":"Manager"}', true);

